{"issues":[{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"10035","self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/latest/issue/10035","key":"AP-2","fields":{"summary":"CSV Backlog Ingestion","issuetype":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issuetype/10037","id":"10037","description":"Stories track functionality or features expressed as user goals.","iconUrl":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10315?size=medium","name":"Story","subtask":false,"avatarId":10315,"entityId":"a9502e0d-867b-4e13-9c45-261e65fe910f","hierarchyLevel":0},"parent":{"id":"10033","key":"AP-1","self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/10033","fields":{"summary":"Core Scheduling Engine MVP","status":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/status/10066","description":"","iconUrl":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/","name":"To Do","id":"10066","statusCategory":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/statuscategory/2","id":2,"key":"new","colorName":"blue-gray","name":"To Do"}},"priority":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/priority/1","iconUrl":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/images/icons/priorities/highest_new.svg","name":"Highest","id":"1"},"issuetype":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issuetype/10035","id":"10035","description":"Epics track collections of related bugs, stories, and tasks.","iconUrl":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10307?size=medium","name":"Epic","subtask":false,"avatarId":10307,"entityId":"21b28705-2e2b-43f3-95af-c2d445b6d5a2","hierarchyLevel":1}}},"creator":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/user?accountId=712020%3A87eb1729-fc17-4029-97ee-3780fbdbe2e9","accountId":"712020:87eb1729-fc17-4029-97ee-3780fbdbe2e9","emailAddress":"ataiassistant@gmail.com","avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1e948a9d865d5779585b350f8f9a0c0c?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAA-2.png","24x24":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1e948a9d865d5779585b350f8f9a0c0c?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAA-2.png","16x16":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1e948a9d865d5779585b350f8f9a0c0c?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAA-2.png","32x32":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1e948a9d865d5779585b350f8f9a0c0c?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAA-2.png"},"displayName":"AI Assistant","active":true,"timeZone":"Europe/Minsk","accountType":"atlassian"},"components":[],"created":"2025-12-10T13:34:19.535+0300","description":"h2. Overview\r\n\r\n*Purpose*: This solution design document provides a comprehensive technical architecture for implementing CSV Backlog Ingestion functionality. The system will parse CSV files containing task details and convert raw data into structured Task objects for downstream processing in the Gantt Schedule Calculation System.\r\n\r\n*Usage*: This design serves as the blueprint for implementing the CSV parser component, ensuring alignment with existing system architecture and technical requirements.\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nh2. Business Context\r\n\r\nh3. Problem Statement\r\n\r\n{quote}\r\nCurrently, project managers and system administrators need to manually process CSV backlog files to extract task information. Raw CSV data must be converted into structured Task objects that can be processed by the scheduling engine. Without automated parsing, this process is error-prone, time-consuming, and lacks validation for data quality issues such as missing required fields or invalid estimates.\r\n{quote}\r\n\r\nThe business problem this solution addresses is the need for automated, reliable CSV file ingestion that validates data quality and converts unstructured CSV rows into standardized Task objects ready for scheduling calculations.\r\n\r\nh3. Business Objectives\r\n\r\n*Objective 1*: Automate CSV file parsing to eliminate manual data conversion and reduce human error in backlog ingestion.\r\n\r\n*Objective 2*: Ensure data quality through validation rules that identify and handle missing or invalid data gracefully, with clear logging for troubleshooting.\r\n\r\n*Objective 3*: Support flexible estimate formats (Story Points vs Days/Hours) based on team configuration, accommodating different workflow methodologies.\r\n\r\nh3. Success Criteria\r\n\r\n*Criterion 1*: System successfully parses valid CSV files with 100% accuracy, converting all valid rows to Task objects.\r\n\r\n*Criterion 2*: Invalid or missing data is handled gracefully with appropriate warnings logged, and processing continues for valid rows.\r\n\r\n*Criterion 3*: Estimate validation correctly enforces business rules (Story Points: 1,2,3,5,8 only; Days/Hours: decimal allowed with conversion to hours) based on configuration.\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nh2. Solution Architecture\r\n\r\nh3. High-Level Architecture\r\n\r\n{code:markdown}\r\n```mermaid\r\ngraph TB\r\n    subgraph \"Input Layer\"\r\n        A[CSV File Input]\r\n        B[dmtools CLI Command]\r\n    end\r\n    subgraph \"Processing Layer\"\r\n        C[File Validator]\r\n        D[CSV Parser]\r\n        E[Data Validator]\r\n        F[Estimate Processor]\r\n        G[Task Builder]\r\n    end\r\n    subgraph \"Output Layer\"\r\n        H[Task Array]\r\n        I[Structured Logger]\r\n    end\r\n    B -->|--input flag| C\r\n    A --> C\r\n    C -->|Valid File| D\r\n    D --> E\r\n    E --> F\r\n    F --> G\r\n    G --> H\r\n    E -->|Warnings| I\r\n    F -->|Warnings| I\r\n    C -->|Error| I\r\n```\r\n{code}\r\n\r\n*Description*: The high-level architecture consists of three main layers: Input Layer (CSV file and CLI command interface), Processing Layer (validation, parsing, and transformation components), and Output Layer (structured Task objects and logging). The flow ensures file validation occurs before parsing, data validation happens during processing, and all warnings/errors are logged through a structured logger.\r\n\r\nh3. Component Architecture\r\n\r\n{code:markdown}\r\n```mermaid\r\nflowchart TD\r\n    Start([CLI Command with --input]) --> ValidateFile{File Exists & Readable?}\r\n    ValidateFile -->|No| Error1[Display Error Message]\r\n    ValidateFile -->|Yes| ParseCSV[Parse CSV with csv-parse]\r\n    ParseCSV -->|Parse Error| Error2[Handle Parse Error]\r\n    ParseCSV -->|Success| IterateRows[Iterate CSV Rows]\r\n    IterateRows --> ValidateRow{ID & Title Present?}\r\n    ValidateRow -->|No| LogWarning[Log Warning with Row Number]\r\n    ValidateRow -->|Yes| ValidateEstimate{Estimate Valid?}\r\n    ValidateEstimate -->|Missing/Invalid| DefaultEstimate[Default to 1, Log Warning]\r\n    ValidateEstimate -->|Valid| ProcessEstimate[Process Estimate by Config]\r\n    DefaultEstimate --> BuildTask[Build Task Object]\r\n    ProcessEstimate --> BuildTask\r\n    BuildTask --> AddToArray[Add to Task Array]\r\n    LogWarning --> NextRow{More Rows?}\r\n    AddToArray --> NextRow\r\n    NextRow -->|Yes| IterateRows\r\n    NextRow -->|No| Summary[Display Summary: Skipped X out of Y]\r\n    Summary --> End([Return Task Array])\r\n    Error1 --> End\r\n    Error2 --> End\r\n```\r\n{code}\r\n\r\n*Description*: The component architecture details the step-by-step processing flow. The system validates file existence first, then parses the CSV. Each row is validated for required fields (ID, Title), and estimates are validated based on configuration rules. Invalid rows are skipped with warnings, while valid rows are converted to Task objects. A summary is provided at the end showing processing statistics.\r\n\r\nh3. Data Architecture\r\n\r\n{code:markdown}\r\n```mermaid\r\nerDiagram\r\n    CSV_FILE ||--o{ CSV_ROW : contains\r\n    CSV_ROW ||--o| TASK : transforms_to\r\n    CONFIG ||--o{ TASK : validates\r\n    CSV_ROW {\r\n        string ID\r\n        string Title\r\n        string Estimate\r\n        string Component\r\n        string ParentId\r\n        string IssueType\r\n    }\r\n    TASK {\r\n        string id PK\r\n        string title\r\n        number estimate\r\n        string component\r\n        string parentId\r\n        string issueType\r\n    }\r\n    CONFIG {\r\n        string estimateType\r\n        number hoursPerDay\r\n        array validStoryPoints\r\n    }\r\n```\r\n{code}\r\n\r\n*Description*: The data architecture shows the transformation from CSV rows to Task objects. CSV rows contain raw string data that must be parsed and validated. The Task interface aligns with the broader Task model from technical requirements, including core fields (id, title, estimate) and optional fields (component, parentId, issueType). Configuration drives estimate validation rules and conversion logic.\r\n\r\nh3. Integration Architecture\r\n\r\n{code:markdown}\r\n```mermaid\r\nsequenceDiagram\r\n    participant CLI as dmtools CLI\r\n    participant Validator as File Validator\r\n    participant Parser as CSV Parser\r\n    participant Validator2 as Data Validator\r\n    participant Processor as Estimate Processor\r\n    participant Builder as Task Builder\r\n    participant Logger as Structured Logger\r\n    participant Output as Task Array\r\n\r\n    CLI->>Validator: Execute with --input flag\r\n    Validator->>Validator: Check file existence\r\n    Validator->>Validator: Check file readability\r\n    Validator-->>CLI: File valid or error\r\n    CLI->>Parser: Provide file path\r\n    Parser->>Parser: Read CSV file\r\n    Parser->>Parser: Parse with csv-parse library\r\n    Parser->>Validator2: Stream parsed rows\r\n    loop For each row\r\n        Validator2->>Validator2: Check ID present\r\n        Validator2->>Validator2: Check Title present\r\n        alt Missing required field\r\n            Validator2->>Logger: Log warning with row number\r\n        else Valid row\r\n            Validator2->>Processor: Provide Estimate value\r\n            Processor->>Processor: Validate by config type\r\n            alt Invalid estimate\r\n                Processor->>Logger: Log default applied\r\n                Processor->>Processor: Set estimate to 1\r\n            end\r\n            Processor->>Builder: Provide validated data\r\n            Builder->>Builder: Create Task object\r\n            Builder->>Output: Add Task to array\r\n        end\r\n    end\r\n    Parser->>Logger: Provide summary statistics\r\n    Logger->>CLI: Display summary\r\n    Output-->>CLI: Return Task array\r\n```\r\n{code}\r\n\r\n*Description*: The integration architecture shows the sequence of interactions between components. The CLI initiates the process, file validation occurs first, then CSV parsing streams rows to the data validator. Each row is validated, estimates are processed according to configuration, and valid rows are transformed into Task objects. Warnings and errors are logged throughout the process, and a summary is provided at completion.\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nh2. Technical Design\r\n\r\nh3. Technology Stack\r\n\r\n*Runtime & Language:*\r\n* Node.js (LTS v18+) - Runtime environment for CLI execution\r\n* TypeScript 5.x - Type-safe implementation with strict mode\r\n\r\n*Libraries & Frameworks:*\r\n* csv-parse - CSV parsing library for reading and parsing CSV files\r\n* dmtools CLI - Command-line interface framework for argument parsing and file input handling\r\n* Structured Logger - Logging framework for warning messages and error reporting\r\n\r\n*Tools & Infrastructure:*\r\n* TypeScript Compiler - Type checking and compilation\r\n* ESLint/Prettier - Code quality and formatting\r\n* Jest/Vitest - Testing framework for unit tests\r\n\r\nh3. Design Patterns\r\n\r\n*Pattern 1: Pipeline Pattern* - The CSV processing follows a pipeline where data flows through validation, parsing, transformation, and output stages. Each stage handles a specific concern, making the system modular and testable.\r\n\r\n*Pattern 2: Strategy Pattern* - Estimate validation and processing uses a strategy pattern based on configuration (Story Points strategy vs Days/Hours strategy). This allows different validation rules and conversion logic to be applied based on team configuration.\r\n\r\n*Pattern 3: Builder Pattern* - Task objects are constructed using a builder pattern that ensures all required fields are present and optional fields are handled appropriately. This provides flexibility for future Task model extensions.\r\n\r\nh3. Security Considerations\r\n\r\n*Security measure 1*: File path validation prevents directory traversal attacks by ensuring the provided file path is within allowed directories and doesn't contain malicious path components.\r\n\r\n*Security measure 2*: File size limits prevent memory exhaustion attacks by restricting the maximum CSV file size that can be processed.\r\n\r\n*Security measure 3*: Input sanitization ensures that parsed CSV data doesn't contain executable code or injection vectors before being processed.\r\n\r\nh3. Performance Considerations\r\n\r\n*Performance optimization 1*: Streaming CSV parsing processes rows incrementally rather than loading the entire file into memory, enabling processing of large CSV files efficiently.\r\n\r\n*Performance optimization 2*: Early validation skips invalid rows immediately without full processing, reducing unnecessary computation for malformed data.\r\n\r\n*Performance optimization 3*: Lazy evaluation of optional fields defers processing until needed, improving initial parsing speed.\r\n\r\nh3. Scalability Considerations\r\n\r\n*Scalability approach 1*: The streaming parser architecture supports processing CSV files of varying sizes without memory constraints, scaling from small files (dozens of rows) to large files (thousands of rows).\r\n\r\n*Scalability approach 2*: Modular component design allows for future extension to support additional input formats (XLSX, JSON) without major architectural changes.\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nh2. Development Scope Decomposition\r\n\r\nh3. Decomposition Strategy\r\n\r\n*Important: This feature is manageable as a single implementation unit. The scope is focused on CSV parsing, validation, and Task object creation, which can be completed within a single development iteration. No decomposition into separate components is required.*\r\n\r\n*Approach: Single Solution Design*\r\n\r\nThe CSV Backlog Ingestion feature is self-contained and has clear boundaries:\r\n* Input: CSV file path via CLI\r\n* Processing: Parse, validate, transform\r\n* Output: Array of Task objects\r\n\r\nThe feature is tightly coupled (parsing, validation, and transformation must work together) and cannot be meaningfully split into independent components. Artificial separation would create unnecessary overhead and complexity.\r\n\r\nh3. Component 1: CSV Backlog Ingestion (Complete Feature)\r\n\r\n*Scope*: Complete implementation of CSV file parsing, data validation, estimate processing, and Task object creation.\r\n\r\n*Task 1.1: File Input and Validation*\r\n\r\n*Acceptance Criteria:*\r\n* AC1: CLI command accepts --input flag with file path argument\r\n* AC2: System validates file exists and is readable before parsing\r\n* AC3: Appropriate error message displayed if --input flag is missing or file doesn't exist\r\n* AC4: Error handling gracefully handles file permission issues\r\n\r\n*Dependencies*: dmtools CLI framework, file system access\r\n\r\n*Estimated Effort*: 2 story points\r\n\r\n*Task 1.2: CSV Parsing Implementation*\r\n\r\n*Acceptance Criteria:*\r\n* AC1: System uses csv-parse library to parse CSV file\r\n* AC2: CSV parsing handles standard CSV format with headers\r\n* AC3: System correctly extracts ID, Title, and Estimate columns\r\n* AC4: Parsing handles edge cases (quoted fields, escaped commas, empty rows)\r\n\r\n*Dependencies*: csv-parse library, Task 1.1 (file validation)\r\n\r\n*Estimated Effort*: 3 story points\r\n\r\n*Task 1.3: Data Validation and Row Processing*\r\n\r\n*Acceptance Criteria:*\r\n* AC1: System skips rows with missing ID or Title fields\r\n* AC2: Structured logger logs warnings for each skipped row with row number and missing fields\r\n* AC3: System provides summary at end showing \"Skipped X rows out of Y total\"\r\n* AC4: CLI flag allows suppression of warning messages\r\n\r\n*Dependencies*: Structured logger, Task 1.2 (CSV parsing)\r\n\r\n*Estimated Effort*: 3 story points\r\n\r\n*Task 1.4: Estimate Validation and Processing*\r\n\r\n*Acceptance Criteria:*\r\n* AC1: System validates estimates based on configuration (Story Points: 1,2,3,5,8 only; Days/Hours: decimal allowed)\r\n* AC2: Invalid estimates (non-numeric, negative, zero, >= 7 days, >= 13 story points) are rejected and defaulted to 1\r\n* AC3: Default value application is logged when estimate is missing or invalid\r\n* AC4: Days/weeks are converted to hours based on 8 hours per day (configurable)\r\n* AC5: Story points validation enforces allowed values only\r\n\r\n*Dependencies*: Configuration system, Task 1.3 (data validation)\r\n\r\n*Estimated Effort*: 5 story points\r\n\r\n*Task 1.5: Task Interface and Object Creation*\r\n\r\n*Acceptance Criteria:*\r\n* AC1: Task interface defined in src/models/Task.ts aligned with broader Task model\r\n* AC2: Interface includes core fields: id (string), title (string), estimate (number)\r\n* AC3: Interface includes optional fields: component, parentId, issueType\r\n* AC4: System creates Task objects from validated CSV rows\r\n* AC5: Task objects are returned as an array in memory\r\n\r\n*Dependencies*: Task model definition, Task 1.4 (estimate processing)\r\n\r\n*Estimated Effort*: 2 story points\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nh2. Development Workflow\r\n\r\n{code:markdown}\r\n```mermaid\r\ngraph LR\r\n    A[Planning] --> B[Design]\r\n    B --> C[Development]\r\n    C --> D[Code Review]\r\n    D --> E[Testing]\r\n    E --> F{Pass?}\r\n    F -->|Yes| G[Deploy]\r\n    F -->|No| C\r\n    G --> H[Monitor]\r\n```\r\n{code}\r\n\r\n*Description*: Standard development workflow applies: planning and design phase, implementation, code review, comprehensive testing (unit tests for parsing logic, validation rules, and edge cases), and deployment. Monitoring ensures the feature works correctly in production with real CSV files.\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nh2. Dependencies & Risks\r\n\r\nh3. Dependencies\r\n\r\n*External Dependency 1*: csv-parse library availability and maintenance - Impact if delayed: Feature cannot be implemented without alternative parsing solution\r\n\r\n*External Dependency 2*: dmtools CLI framework compatibility - Impact if delayed: CLI integration may require adaptation if framework changes\r\n\r\n*Internal Dependency 1*: Task model definition in src/models/Task.ts - Impact if delayed: Task interface must be finalized before object creation can be completed\r\n\r\nh3. Risks & Mitigation\r\n\r\n*Risk 1*: CSV format variations may not be handled correctly\r\n*Probability*: Medium\r\n*Impact*: Medium\r\n*Mitigation*: Comprehensive testing with various CSV formats, support for common variations (quoted fields, different delimiters), clear error messages for unsupported formats\r\n\r\n*Risk 2*: Estimate validation rules may be too strict or too lenient\r\n*Probability*: Low\r\n*Impact*: Low\r\n*Mitigation*: Configuration-based validation allows adjustment without code changes, default to 1 provides safe fallback, logging helps identify validation issues\r\n\r\n*Risk 3*: Large CSV files may cause performance issues\r\n*Probability*: Low\r\n*Impact*: Medium\r\n*Mitigation*: Streaming parser architecture processes rows incrementally, performance testing with large files (5000+ rows) to validate approach\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nh2. Testing Strategy\r\n\r\nh3. Unit Testing\r\n\r\n*Coverage target*: 90% code coverage for parsing, validation, and transformation logic\r\n\r\n*Key areas*:\r\n* CSV parsing with various formats (standard, quoted fields, escaped characters)\r\n* Row validation (missing ID, missing Title, both present)\r\n* Estimate validation (Story Points: valid/invalid values, Days/Hours: conversion logic, invalid inputs)\r\n* Task object creation with all field combinations\r\n* Error handling for file access issues\r\n\r\nh3. Integration Testing\r\n\r\n*Scope*: End-to-end CSV file processing from CLI command to Task array output\r\n\r\n*Key scenarios*:\r\n* Valid CSV file with all required fields produces correct Task array\r\n* CSV file with missing fields produces warnings and skips invalid rows\r\n* CSV file with invalid estimates applies defaults and logs appropriately\r\n* Missing --input flag produces appropriate error message\r\n* Invalid file path produces appropriate error message\r\n* Large CSV file (1000+ rows) processes successfully\r\n\r\nh3. End-to-End Testing\r\n\r\n*Scope*: Full workflow from CSV file ingestion through to Task array ready for scheduling engine\r\n\r\n*Key user journeys*:\r\n* User provides valid CSV file via CLI, receives Task array with all valid rows processed\r\n* User provides CSV with data quality issues, receives Task array with warnings logged and invalid rows skipped\r\n* User provides CSV with various estimate formats, receives correctly validated and converted estimates\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nh2. Deployment Plan\r\n\r\nh3. Environments\r\n\r\n*Development*: Local development environment for implementation and initial testing\r\n\r\n*Staging*: Integration environment for testing with real CSV file formats and team configurations\r\n\r\n*Production*: Production deployment as part of Gantt Schedule Calculation System CLI tool\r\n\r\nh3. Deployment Strategy\r\n\r\n*Approach*: Direct deployment as CLI tool feature, no separate service deployment required\r\n\r\n*Rollback plan*: Feature can be disabled via feature flag or removed in subsequent release if issues arise\r\n\r\n*Monitoring*: Log monitoring for parsing errors, validation warnings, and performance metrics (processing time, rows processed, rows skipped)\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nh2. Documentation Requirements\r\n\r\n*API Documentation*: TSDoc comments for all exported functions and interfaces, including parameters, return values, and usage examples\r\n\r\n*User Documentation*: CLI usage guide explaining --input flag, CSV format requirements, estimate validation rules, and warning suppression flag\r\n\r\n*Technical Documentation*: Architecture documentation explaining component interactions, data flow, and extension points for future input formats\r\n\r\n*Runbooks*: Troubleshooting guide for common CSV parsing issues, validation errors, and performance problems\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nh2. Timeline & Milestones\r\n\r\n*Milestone 1*: File Input and Validation - Week 1\r\n\r\n*Milestone 2*: CSV Parsing and Basic Validation - Week 1-2\r\n\r\n*Milestone 3*: Estimate Processing and Task Creation - Week 2\r\n\r\n*Milestone 4*: Testing and Documentation - Week 2-3\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nh2. Open Questions\r\n\r\n*Question 1*: Should the system support CSV files with different column orders, or require exact column names? - *Owner*: Product Owner - *Status*: Pending\r\n\r\n*Question 2*: What is the maximum CSV file size that should be supported? - *Owner*: Technical Lead - *Status*: Pending\r\n\r\n*Question 3*: Should the system support CSV files with BOM (Byte Order Mark) for UTF-8 encoding? - *Owner*: Technical Lead - *Status*: Pending\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nh2. Appendix\r\n\r\nh3. References\r\n\r\n*[Reference 1]*: Technical Requirements Specification - docs/technical-requirements.md\r\n\r\n*[Reference 2]*: Business Requirements Specification - docs/business-requirements.md\r\n\r\n*[Reference 3]*: Solution Design Template - https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AC/pages/25133058/Solution+design+template\r\n\r\nh3. Glossary\r\n\r\n*Task*: A structured object representing a work item with id, title, estimate, and optional metadata fields\r\n\r\n*Story Points*: Agile estimation unit with allowed values of 1, 2, 3, 5, or 8\r\n\r\n*Estimate*: Effort estimation for a task, can be in Story Points or Days/Hours format\r\n\r\n*CSV Parser*: Component responsible for reading and parsing CSV file format into structured data\r\n\r\n*Structured Logger*: Logging system that outputs warnings and errors in a structured format for analysis","reporter":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/user?accountId=712020%3A87eb1729-fc17-4029-97ee-3780fbdbe2e9","accountId":"712020:87eb1729-fc17-4029-97ee-3780fbdbe2e9","emailAddress":"ataiassistant@gmail.com","avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1e948a9d865d5779585b350f8f9a0c0c?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAA-2.png","24x24":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1e948a9d865d5779585b350f8f9a0c0c?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAA-2.png","16x16":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1e948a9d865d5779585b350f8f9a0c0c?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAA-2.png","32x32":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1e948a9d865d5779585b350f8f9a0c0c?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAA-2.png"},"displayName":"AI Assistant","active":true,"timeZone":"Europe/Minsk","accountType":"atlassian"},"fixVersions":[],"priority":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/priority/3","iconUrl":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/images/icons/priorities/medium_new.svg","name":"Medium","id":"3"},"labels":["AI_solution","ai_generated"],"attachment":[],"issuelinks":[],"updated":"2025-12-16T14:12:25.010+0300","status":{"self":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/status/10069","description":"","iconUrl":"https://kidblendapp.atlassian.net/","name":"IN REVIEW","id":"10069","statusCategory":{"self":"https://kidblend